  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader, I want the message layout to match legacy at three points: the signature is indented like the text, the text has a right margin, and quote rules are no heavier than the separators between replies. That way a long topic reads as calmly as in HFR+. (Operator feedback, 2026-11-17, device screenshots of SwiftHFR and legacy on the same page.)\n\n### Observed (SwiftHFR, dev-swift) vs legacy @ 87fe0d1c\n\n| | SwiftHFR | Legacy |\n|---|---|---|\n| **(A) Signature** | Its text starts at the screen edge, left of the message text | Indented like the text. The dotted rule above it still starts at the edge |\n| **(B) Right margin** | The text runs to the right edge (« se p|oser » is cut against the edge) | A right margin, from `padding-right` / `margin-right` in `SuperHFRplus/Assets/HTML/style-liste-*.css` (e.g. `style-liste-light.css:225, 263, 506`) |\n| **(D) Quote rules** | A full-width rule above and below each quote block, as thick as or thicker than the separator between replies | No such rules: the quote shows its left bar only |\n\nThe signature rules are `span.signature` in `style-liste-dark.css:45-65` and `style-liste-light.css:79-99`; the light and oled sheets have the same blocks.\n\n### Scope\n\n- **(A)** Indent the signature text to the message text's left inset. The dotted rule above it keeps starting at the edge (operator).\n- **(B)** Add the right margin from legacy's sheet: cite the exact value used, per theme sheet if they differ.\n- **(D)** **Parity:** remove the rules above and below quotes (operator option 1).\n  - If removing them hurts readability in a theme, keep a rule no thicker or more contrasted than the reply separator (operator option 2). Say which option was taken and why in the PR.\n  - A rule inside a reply must never be heavier than a rule between replies.\n- Every theme, light, dark and oled, and the density settings.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- Tests on the generated CSS/HTML (`TopicHTMLBuilder` and the reader stylesheet):\n  - the signature's left inset equals the text inset;\n  - the dotted rule starts at 0;\n  - the right padding has the cited value;\n  - no quote rule, or one at most as thick as the separator.\n- An app-hosted WebKit test measuring (A) and (B) in a real `WKWebView`.\n- Tests fail without the change.\n- A `### Ledger` `changelog` entry if a legacy difference is fixed, citing legacy file:line.\n\n### Device check (for the #893 general review)\n\nThe same page as the screenshots, in dark and light.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
